  "/resources/symptom-guides/cramps-but-no-period": {
    "collection": "symptom-guides",
    "description": "Cramping without a period can mean ovulation, a cyst, ectopic pregnancy, or more. Learn what each pattern feels like and when to seek care.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Can stress cause cramps without a period?",
        "a": "Stress can affect cycle timing for some people. If cramps show up during a stressful cycle, write down the date, pain location, period timing, sleep, illness, and any pregnancy concern. Do not use stress as the only explanation if pain is severe, new, or worrying."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can IBS or digestive issues cause cramps that feel like period cramps?",
        "a": "Yes. The lower abdominal cramping of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) can closely mimic menstrual cramps in sensation and location. IBS cramping often correlates with bowel changes (diarrhea, constipation, or both) and may worsen in the luteal phase when progesterone slows gut motility. Logging bowel symptoms alongside pelvic pain helps clarify the pattern."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is it an emergency if I have one-sided cramps and a positive pregnancy test?",
        "a": "Yes, treat it as urgent. One-sided pelvic pain with a positive pregnancy test can be a sign of ectopic pregnancy or another urgent problem. Go to an emergency room or urgent care immediately. Do not wait."
      },
      {
        "q": "How many days of cramps without a period should I wait before seeing a doctor?",
        "a": "There is no single right answer. Ask a clinician if cramps last more than a few days without a period, get worse, come with fever or unusual discharge, or happen with a missed period and positive pregnancy test. If you are worried, it is okay to ask for care."
      }
    ],
    "metaDescription": "Cramping without a period can mean ovulation, a cyst, ectopic pregnancy, or more. Learn what each pattern feels like and when to seek care.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-04-28",
    "routePath": "/resources/symptom-guides/cramps-but-no-period",
    "seoTitle": "Cramps But No Period: Causes and When to See a Doctor",
    "slug": "cramps-but-no-period",
    "title": "Cramps But No Period: Causes and When to See a Doctor",
    "updatedAt": "2026-07-01"
  },
