        "q": "Does the menstrual cycle affect endurance performance?",
        "a": "Core temperature rises 0.3-0.5°C in the luteal phase due to progesterone. In heat-sensitive endurance events, this can affect performance and increase perceived effort. In thermoneutral conditions, the effect on endurance capacity is less clear. Hydration and cooling strategies may be more important in the luteal phase."
