  "/resources/guides/how-to-track-irregular-menstrual-cycle": {
    "collection": "guides",
    "description": "Irregular cycles are harder to track but more important to document. What counts as irregular, how to build a useful baseline, and when to see a provider.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "How irregular is too irregular?",
        "a": "A general guideline: if cycles consistently fall outside the 21 to 35 day range, vary by more than nine days between cycles, or if periods are absent for more than 90 days, discuss findings with a healthcare provider. This is educational guidance only, individual circumstances vary and a healthcare provider can give personalized evaluation."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does stress actually cause irregular periods?",
        "a": "Yes, in some cases. The hypothalamic-pituitary-ovarian axis, the hormonal system that regulates the menstrual cycle, is responsive to physiological and psychological stress. Significant physical or emotional stress can suppress or delay ovulation, which in turn affects cycle timing. However, stress is not the only cause of irregular cycles, and attributing irregularity solely to stress can delay evaluation of other conditions."
      },
      {
        "q": "Will tracking help if my cycles are very irregular?",
        "a": "Yes, but the goal shifts. With very irregular cycles, tracking does not produce accurate period predictions. What it does produce is a documented record of your actual pattern, which is useful for healthcare consultations, for identifying any triggers (stress, illness, travel, dietary changes) that correlate with particularly irregular periods, and for detecting trends over time."
      }
    ],
    "metaDescription": "Irregular cycles are harder to track but more important to document. What counts as irregular, how to build a useful baseline, and when to see a provider.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-03-21",
    "routePath": "/resources/guides/how-to-track-irregular-menstrual-cycle",
    "seoTitle": "How to Track an Irregular Menstrual Cycle",
    "slug": "how-to-track-irregular-menstrual-cycle",
    "title": "How to Track an Irregular Menstrual Cycle",
    "updatedAt": "2026-03-21"
  },
